{
  "_comment": [
    "THE PARTS CATALOGUE — what a device IS, as a matter of the metal.",
    "",
    "A scan says a 54641D answered on TCPIP::44.44.44.222::gpib7,6::INSTR. It",
    "does not say the instrument has four BNCs, a sixteen-way logic pod and an",
    "EXT TRIG on the front of it, because nothing on the wire carries that. So",
    "the panel is DECLARED here, once per model, and every bench that discovers",
    "that model inherits it.",
    "",
    "NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A MEASUREMENT. Each part names the manual it was",
    "read out of in `source`, and a declared terminal is never given an MQTT",
    "topic — a connector is not a capture point, and drawing it as one would",
    "put a probe circle on a socket no probe is on.",
    "",
    "THE JOIN IS manufacturer + model, NOT THE SERIAL. Two 33220As on one bench",
    "are two instances of one part. Where a manufacturer string varies between",
    "scans ('Agilent', 'AGILENT TECHNOLOGIES', 'Keysight'), `manufacturer_aka`",
    "lists what has actually been seen rather than normalising the scan.",
    "",
    "SIDES are input, output and connection — the same three the simulation",
    "model draws down the left edge, down the right, and along the bottom.",
    "DOMAINS are the eight the internals view stacks: audio, video, midi,",
    "signal, network, control, clock, power.",
    "",
    "`build_bim_parts.py` reads this and writes, per part, two files into",
    "library/: a `.bim.json` frame the Simulation window imports as a library",
    "part, and a `.ifc` — IFC4, ISO 16739 — which is the interchange copy any",
    "other BIM tool can open. Neither is edited by hand."
  ],
